From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scfb: no xf86DisableRandR() for a rotated screen

xorg-server 21.1.25 (FreeBSD's quarterly packages, November 2026) no
longer has xf86DisableRandR(), and scfb calls it when Option "Rotate" is
set: Xorg ends with ld-elf's "Undefined symbol xf86DisableRandR" right
after "Enabling Driver Rotation, disabling RandR", the console left in
graphics mode. Without the call RandR stays on with the one mode;
the driver offers it no rotations, so clients cannot turn the screen.

---
diff --git a/src/scfb_driver.c b/src/scfb_driver.c
index ac3ca97..73906dd 100644
--- a/src/scfb_driver.c
+++ b/src/scfb_driver.c
@@ -839,7 +839,6 @@ ScfbScreenInit(SCREEN_INIT_ARGS_DECL)
 	if (fPtr->rotate) {
 		xf86DrvMsg(pScrn->scrnIndex, X_INFO, "Enabling Driver Rotation, "
 		    "disabling RandR\n");
-		xf86DisableRandR();
 		if (pScrn->bitsPerPixel == 24)
 			xf86DrvMsg(pScrn->scrnIndex, X_WARNING,
 			    "Rotation might be broken in 24 bpp\n");
